    "<b>The explanation goes here:</b>\n",
    "\n",
    "A1) We can differentiate vessels by their thickness, continuity, and branching structure—main vessels are thicker and smoother, while sub-branches are thin and irregular.\n",
    "Deep models also capture contrast and directional continuity to distinguish them.\n",
    "\n",
    "A2) Our dataset contains low-contrast and extremely thin vessels, making sub-branches almost invisible.\n",
    "This causes ambiguity because many small vessels blend into the background or resemble noise.\n",
    "\n",
    "A3) Applying Grad-CAM will highlight where the model focuses, mostly on thicker main vessels rather than fine branches.\n",
    "This happens because the final convolutional layers respond more strongly to coarse/high-contrast structures.\n"
   ]
